  "details": "Right now, any and all avatar or world settings, persistent or not, have to be customised on a per device level.\n\nThis makes it really annoying for those of us who travel a lot and use VRChat accross multiple devices (e.g. Desktop, Steam Deck, Oculus, Laptop) to do so, because we are forced to repeatedly change the same avatar and world settings on every device. This starts as a slight inconvenience at first but quickly becomes a very time consuming annoyance when the avatars you wear or the worlds you visit have ton of settings.\n\nThe solution I'm rooting for here is for VRChat to save settings to cloud everytime they are changed, alongside the device and time stamp of the change, so that later when the user loads the same avatar or world on a different device, VRChat can either prompt the user to select which cloud save they want to load settings from, listing the device, time stamp and possibly other useful information about the cloud save.\n\nShould such or similar system be ever implemented to VRChat, I believe that:\n\n• The game should never make automated decision about which cloud save to use or select, unless explicitly specified otherwise by the end user. \n\n• Some settings such as performance and graphics settings, should be excluded from cloud sync. These settings will inevitably differ across devices. (i.e loading high-fidelity settings optimized for a high-end desktop onto a mobile device like the Steam Deck would create performance issues)\n\nThanks for making it to the end of my post, please let me and VRChat know what you think about this idea by leaving a comment below.",
